=== HINT 1 ===
_Generic(expr, type1: val1, type2: val2, default: val3)
The controlling expression is only type-checked, NOT evaluated at runtime.

=== HINT 2 ===
#define TYPE_NAME(x) _Generic((x),   \
    int:    "int",                   \
    long:   "long",                  \
    ...                              \
    default: "unknown")

=== HINT 3 ===
Pointer types must be listed exactly:
  char*: "char*"
  void*: "void*"
Note: char* and void* are different association entries.

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
#define TYPE_NAME(x) _Generic((x),  \
    int:    "int",                  \
    long:   "long",                 \
    float:  "float",                \
    double: "double",               \
    char*:  "char*",                \
    void*:  "void*",                \
    default: "unknown")
